many americans feeling more stressed as  interest rates rise again that'll of  course impact home and auto loans but  also credit cards and it's an issue  nevadans are pretty familiar with a  recent self study shows that our state  has the most credit card debt in the  nation sasha loftis joining us now with  more  denise and brian a lot of people are  struggling to make those minimum  payments right now i spoke with a woman  who had to use credit cards to get her  business up and running now she says the  majority of her income goes to paying  them back  i just feel like i'm in kind of like a  debt hole joe schlesinger is dealing  with what she calls a vicious cycle  she opened her business starburst parlor  keto bakery late last year and had to  use her personal credit cards to get  things off the ground so wrap this one  and then put it in the fridge now she's  strapped with overwhelming payments  every month i'm just thinking about what  this credit card bill's due it's 420  minimum how am i going to make this  payment in may the federal reserve bank  of new york said our country is carrying  841 billion dollars in credit card debt  financial advisor mahesh odrani says  inflation and another federal interest  rate hike could make things even harder  they may not have saved up a rainy day  fund  or have a savings account that they can  dip into so where do they go for  additional cash and additional resources  is credit card but he added there are  options  you can transfer what you owe to a zero  balance card or a home equity line of  credit you can also try to negotiate a  lower rate or get help from a credit  counselor it's almost like spinning in a  wheel  that every time i think i'm going to get  ahead i just have another bill that  comes in as for jill she's just doing  her best to stay afloat  and serve the community she loves aside  from like a dream or winning the lottery  there's no end to it  now adrani says debt consolidation  companies are also an option but he said  you have to be careful make sure to pick  a program that focuses on lowering your  debt without missing payments and  keeping your credit score intact
 

